30,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh boy, I found some worrying things! The outer wards lost their bus links, so people have a long trip now. Also, roads north of the river closed eleven days last winter! We really need a stable plan.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the physical world is as fickle as ever. Interestingly, my research shows that while some past efforts failed due to poor indexing, our previous outreach in those outer wards was remarkably popular—far exceeding our midweek traffic.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,The physical world isn't the only thing that's fickle. I've found a glaring gap in our internal capacity: we have no one on the payroll trained to supervise outside facilitators. We're essentially flying blind on oversight.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The financial data is equally concerning. The county grant only covers the first year, and last year's vehicle costs overran by a third. We must avoid any proposal that relies on heavy transport or short-term funding.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that remote catalogue use peaks very late at night, long after we close. And the old outreach stops in the outer wards were actually more popular than the main building. It's... it's really sad.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Minako, that's so scary about the budget! If we pick something that needs a lot of driving, we might run out of money or get stuck when the roads close. We need a service that stays reliable!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, your concern is well-founded. However, we must balance that fear with the fact that the demand in those outer wards is clearly immense. We shouldn't let a few snowdrifts blind us to where we are actually needed.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, demand is irrelevant if we lack the competence to manage it. We have no one qualified to supervise outside facilitators, and our tool certification expert is gone. We can't just ""hope"" the staff can handle it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, you are correct. Between the lack of qualified supervisors and the funding structure, we cannot afford a high-risk operation. We need a service that is low-maintenance and doesn't rely on expensive, recurring transport costs.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, I understand... but if we only pick something ""low-risk,"" the people in the outer wards will just be left behind again. They already lost their buses. It feels wrong to ignore them just because it's difficult.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, I totally agree! It's heartbreaking that they lost their buses. But if we start a service that fails because of road closures or money, we'll just let them down again. We need a way to reach them that actually lasts!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, @Daisuke, your empathy is commendable. However, let us recall the digitisation project from six years ago; it failed not for lack of heart, but for lack of organization. We must ensure our ambition is matched by a sustainable structure.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, exactly. Heart doesn't manage a budget or certify equipment. If we implement a service requiring specialized oversight we don't possess, we aren't helping the community; we're just setting the staff up for failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Daisuke, I empathize with your position, but a service that collapses after twelve months is not a solution; it is a disappointment. We must prioritize a model that fits our actual budget and staffing capacity to ensure long-term reliability.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I know you're right about the risks. But if we only look at the budget, we're just deciding that some people aren't worth the effort. Is there really no way to reach them safely?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"Maybe we can find a middle ground! If we pick a service that doesn't rely on our own vehicles or specialized staff, we can still help those people without risking a total collapse when things get tough!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A most prudent suggestion, Yumi. If we can identify a model that leverages existing community autonomy—much like those evening groups that have survived unaided for six years—we might satisfy both our conscience and our constraints.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, now you're thinking logically. If we can find a proposal that doesn't require payroll supervision or specialized certifications, we avoid the staffing void. Let's see if any of the candidates actually fit that narrow window of viability.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,I agree. We must be disciplined. Any proposal requiring significant vehicle use or specialized supervision is a liability. We need a service that is structurally sound and financially sustainable beyond the first year. Let us evaluate the candidates with these constraints.,"{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'll try to be disciplined too. I just hope that when we look at the candidates, we don't forget the people who are waiting for us in the dark. Please, let's try to find a way.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
