59,3,,status,Shion,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Looking at the options, I'm really worried about Option D! With the bus links gone and those road closures, a mobile branch could easily get stuck or become too expensive. We can't risk it failing!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. Option D is a logistical nightmare waiting to happen. Furthermore, Option B reminds me of our failed digitisation attempt; without a rigorous indexing plan, we are simply creating a digital graveyard. We must be more strategic.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is out. We have no one to certify the power tools and no one to supervise the instructors. It's a safety liability we can't manage. That leaves us with B or C.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree with Shion. Option A is a liability, and Option D is financially unsustainable given the vehicle cost overruns and the grant's one-year limit. Option C is the most viable, as it leverages partner organizations.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree that Option D is too risky now. But Option C... it's the only one that actually goes to the people. If we use partners, maybe we can reach the outer wards safely. I vote for C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, you're right! Option C is wonderful because it reaches people where they are, but it doesn't rely on our own cars. It's the perfect way to be kind and reliable at the same time! I vote for C!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, @Daisuke, your alignment is refreshing. Option C mirrors the success of those six-year-old evening groups—autonomous, community-driven, and resilient. It avoids the pitfalls of our past failures and our current constraints. I also vote for C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, for once, your historical parallels are useful. Option C shifts the burden of supervision to the partner organizations, bypassing our lack of qualified staff. It's the only logical choice that doesn't create a management void. I vote for C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Minako,,The consensus is clear. Option C avoids the vehicle costs that would drain our budget in the second year and bypasses our supervision gaps. It is the only sustainable choice. I vote for C.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I'm... I'm glad we could all agree. It makes me feel better knowing we're choosing something that can actually reach the people who've been left behind. I vote for C too.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm just so happy we found a way to help everyone without it being too risky! It feels like we're really taking care of the community together. I'm sticking with my vote for C!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a rare pleasure when logic and empathy converge so seamlessly. By choosing a model that empowers the community rather than one that depends on our own fragile infrastructure, we ensure a legacy of success. My vote remains C.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It's a simple matter of elimination. A and D are liabilities, and B is a waste of time. C is the only option that doesn't rely on a staff competence we simply don't have. My vote is C.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Since we have reached a unanimous agreement based on the financial and personnel constraints we identified, there is no reason to deviate. Option C is the only responsible choice. My vote is C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm just relieved. I was so afraid we'd have to choose between being safe and being fair. Thank you for listening to me. My vote is C.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Yumi,,Yay! I'm so glad we could all agree on something that's both safe and helpful. Let's make these Language Learning Circles the best they can be for everyone! My final vote is C!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. We have avoided the vanity of a flashy project in favor of a sustainable one. It is a victory for pragmatism and a lesson in the value of historical record. My final vote is C.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shion,,"The result is inevitable. We've stripped away the fantasies and the risks, leaving only the one option that doesn't collapse under the weight of our own incompetence. My final vote is C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Minako,,We have carefully weighed the risks and the data. Option C is the only proposal that ensures long-term financial stability and operational viability. My final vote is C.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm just happy we're doing this. I hope the people in the outer wards feel that we haven't forgotten them. My final vote is C.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
